1. Introduction to Programming | What programming is, how programs work, programming languages, compilers, and interpreters
2. Programming Fundamentals | Syntax, statements, variables, constants, data types, and comments
3. Operators and Expressions | Arithmetic operators, comparison operators, logical operators, assignment operators, and operator precedence
4. Input and Output | Receiving user input, displaying output, formatting output, and handling basic user interactions
5. Decision Making | If statements, if-else statements, nested conditions, and switch statements
6. Loops and Repetition | For loops, while loops, do-while loops, nested loops, and controlling loop execution
7. Functions and Modular Programming | Defining functions, parameters, arguments, return values, scope, and reusable code
8. Data Structures | Arrays, lists, strings, tuples, sets, dictionaries, and basic data manipulation
9. Algorithms and Problem-Solving | Breaking down problems, pseudocode, flowcharts, searching, sorting, and algorithm efficiency
10. Object-Oriented Programming | Classes, objects, constructors, methods, encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism
11. Error Handling and Debugging | Syntax errors, runtime errors, logical errors, debugging techniques, and exception handling
12. File Handling | Reading files, writing files, updating files, and working with different file formats
13. Advanced Programming Concepts | Recursion, lambda functions, modules, libraries, higher-order functions, and basic asynchronous programming
14. Working with Data | JSON, data processing, APIs, HTTP requests, and connecting programs to external services
15. Software Development Practices | Code organization, naming conventions, documentation, testing, version control, and writing maintainable code
16. Practical Programming Projects | Building a calculator, quiz application, expense tracker, student management system, and other real-world projects
